{
    "_comment": "IHP SG13G2 130nm BiCMOS PDK abstraction for ALIGN. Phase A: LV CMOS (M1-M5, RVT). Phase B: BEOL TM1/TM2 + HV native 3.3V (Thickox). Phase F: Cmim/CmimVia/PolyRes/EXTBlock/SalBlock/RES added with Direction so gds2lefjson emits them as OBS in black_box LEFs (Phase C deuda). Phase G: V2/V3/V4 retrofit to IHP Vn_a=0.19 / Vn_b=0.22 / Vn_c=0.05 (WidthX/Y=190, SpaceX/Y=220, VencA=50). The Phase F-era placement assertion was rooted in mos.py:_connectNets mixing M1 contact indices with M3 column index when extending the M2 strap; SG13G2's M3.Pitch (560) != M1.Pitch (480) made the mismatch visible, while Mock PDKs hid it because their M3.Pitch==M1.Pitch. Fix is PDK-local in mos.py, no align/ core touched. Layer naming Cmim/CmimVia (instead of native IHP names MIM/Vmim) is intentional: pdk.py dispatches names starting with M to addMetal and V to addVia which require full routing-layer params; the generic add() branch fires for any other initial letter. GDS layer numbers from $IHP_PDK_ROOT/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/klayout/tech/sg13g2.lyp and sg13g2.map.",
